            <section class="spread t-columns"
             data-spread="economy"><h2>economy</h2><div class="prose-slot" lang="en"><p>Nairobi is home to the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nairobi_Securities_Exchange">Nairobi Securities Exchange</a> (NSE), one of Africa's largest <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stock_exchange">stock exchanges</a>. The NSE was officially recognised as an overseas stock exchange by the <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/London_Stock_Exchange">London Stock Exchange</a> in 1953. The exchange is Africa's fourth largest in terms of trading volumes, and fifth largest in terms of Market Capitalization as a percentage of GDP.</p><a class="read" href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nairobi#Economy">Economy ↗</a></div><dl class="sheet" data-slot="sheet"><div class="row r-value"><dt>economy of topic</dt><dd><a href="https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q106020188">economy of Nairobi</a></dd>
    <span class="tools">
